{"causes": ["Şehzade Korkut's birth as the eldest surviving son of Sultan Bayezid II placed him directly in the line of Ottoman succession.", "The Ottoman tradition of fratricide, designed to prevent civil war by eliminating rival princes, created an inherently dangerous environment for all royal heirs.", "Korkut's extensive education and administrative experience as a provincial governor positioned him as a legitimate, albeit ultimately unsuccessful, contender for the sultanate."], "effects": ["Şehzade Korkut's execution in 1513 removed a significant rival, thereby solidifying Sultan Selim I's unchallenged grip on the Ottoman throne.", "His death reinforced the brutal nature of Ottoman succession policies, ensuring that only the most militarily astute and ruthless prince typically survived to rule.", "Korkut's intellectual works on jurisprudence and theology were preserved, contributing to the rich scholarly tradition of the Ottoman Empire despite his political failure."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "bayezid-ii", "sourceName": "Bayezid II", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "targetName": "Şehzade Korkut", "context": "Sultan Bayezid II was the father of Şehzade Korkut, placing him in the direct line of succession."}, {"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "constantinople", "targetName": "Constantinople", "context": "Şehzade Korkut served as regent in Constantinople during his father's illness around 1509."}, {"sourceSlug": "selim-i", "sourceName": "Selim I", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "targetName": "Şehzade Korkut", "context": "Sultan Selim I ordered the execution of his brother Şehzade Korkut on March 13, 1513, to eliminate a rival for the throne."}, {"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "ottoman-succession-struggle", "targetName": "Ottoman Succession Struggle", "context": "Şehzade Korkut actively participated in the dynastic conflicts for the Ottoman throne against his brothers, particularly Selim I, from 1509 to 1513."}, {"sourceSlug": "ottoman-fratricide-law", "sourceName": "Ottoman Fratricide Law", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "targetName": "Şehzade Korkut", "context": "The established Ottoman custom of fratricide profoundly influenced Şehzade Korkut's fate, compelling him into a deadly struggle for survival against his brothers."}], "places": [{"name": "Antalya, Ottoman Empire", "role": "Governorship"}, {"name": "Constantinople, Ottoman Empire", "role": "Regency and Capital"}, {"name": "Bursa, Ottoman Empire", "role": "Execution Site"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Şehzade Korkut", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "şehzade-korkut"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q461500", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9Eehzade_Korkut"], "tags": ["Composers & Musicians", "cultural-diffusion", "cause-and-effect", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Şehzade Korkut's role as a scholarly prince and a contender for the Ottoman throne, whose execution in 1513 solidified Selim I's rule, highlights the brutal mechanisms of imperial succession and the intersection of intellect and power within the Ottoman court.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-19T03:14:15Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44449665893", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Şehzade Korkut was an Ottoman prince who was for a short time the regent for the Ottoman throne. He was the son of the Ottoman Sultan Bayezid II.", "newValue": "Şehzade Korkut (died March 13, 1513) was an Ottoman prince, intellectual, and temporary regent whose life and tragic end illuminate the brutal realities of Ottoman imperial succession during the early 16th century. As the eldest surviving son of Sultan Bayezid II, Korkut was a prominent figure in the dynastic struggles that defined the end of his father's reign and the ascension of his younger brother, Selim I. His significance lies not only in his brief political aspirations but also in his considerable scholarly contributions, marking him as a prince of letters in an era often characterized by military prowess.

Born to Bayezid II, Korkut received a comprehensive education befitting an Ottoman prince, excelling in Islamic theology, law, philosophy, and poetry. He served as the governor of several key Anatolian provinces, including Antalya, a traditional training ground for future sultans. In 1509, during a period of his father's ill health, Korkut briefly acted as regent in Constantinople, a testament to his perceived legitimacy and administrative capabilities. However, his political ambitions were ultimately overshadowed by the more ruthless and militarily adept Selim, who actively sought to depose their father and eliminate all rivals to the throne, as per the Ottoman custom of fratricide to prevent civil war.

Korkut initially withdrew from the succession struggle, even attempting a pilgrimage to Egypt to escape the escalating conflict. However, after his father's deposition in 1512 and Selim I's subsequent ascension, Korkut made a final, ill-fated attempt to rally support in Anatolia, presenting himself as a more just and scholarly alternative to his bellicose brother. This challenge was swiftly crushed by Selim's forces, leading to Korkut's capture and execution near Bursa on March 13, 1513. His death solidified Selim I's undisputed control over the Ottoman Empire, paving the way for Selim's aggressive expansionist policies."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-19T03:14:15Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44449665893", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1467, Amasya"}, {"title": "Musical traditions and compositional innovation", "type": "Idea", "year": "1467, Amasya"}], "newValue": ["Şehzade Korkut's birth as the eldest surviving son of Sultan Bayezid II placed him directly in the line of Ottoman succession.", "The Ottoman tradition of fratricide, designed to prevent civil war by eliminating rival princes, created an inherently dangerous environment for all royal heirs.", "Korkut's extensive education and administrative experience as a provincial governor positioned him as a legitimate, albeit ultimately unsuccessful, contender for the sultanate."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-19T03:14:15Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44449665893", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Created musical compositions of lasting significance", "type": "Idea", "year": "1513-03-13"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1513-03-13"}], "newValue": ["Şehzade Korkut's execution in 1513 removed a significant rival, thereby solidifying Sultan Selim I's unchallenged grip on the Ottoman throne.", "His death reinforced the brutal nature of Ottoman succession policies, ensuring that only the most militarily astute and ruthless prince typically survived to rule.", "Korkut's intellectual works on jurisprudence and theology were preserved, contributing to the rich scholarly tradition of the Ottoman Empire despite his political failure."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-19T03:14:15Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44449665893", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "COMPOSES", "targetSlug": "field-263", "targetName": "Composers & Musicians", "context": "Şehzade Korkut: Musical composition in composers & musicians"}, {"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "medieval", "targetName": "Medieval Era", "context": "Şehzade Korkut was active during the Medieval era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "bayezid-ii", "sourceName": "Bayezid II", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "targetName": "Şehzade Korkut", "context": "Sultan Bayezid II was the father of Şehzade Korkut, placing him in the direct line of succession."}, {"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "constantinople", "targetName": "Constantinople", "context": "Şehzade Korkut served as regent in Constantinople during his father's illness around 1509."}, {"sourceSlug": "selim-i", "sourceName": "Selim I", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "targetName": "Şehzade Korkut", "context": "Sultan Selim I ordered the execution of his brother Şehzade Korkut on March 13, 1513, to eliminate a rival for the throne."}, {"sourceSlug": "şehzade-korkut", "sourceName": "Şehzade Korkut", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "ottoman-succession-struggle", "targetName": "Ottoman Succession Struggle", "context": "Şehzade Korkut activ